WEBVTT

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.420
Episode 11

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.420
Decision<i>!! </i> Enter the
Outer Defensive Lines of Gamilus

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:06.420
( Air date: Dec 15, 1974 )

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:29.550
Saraba Chikyuu yo

00:00:30.250 --> 00:00:33.350
Tabidatsu fune wa...

00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:42.500
...uchuu senkan Yamato

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.220
Space Battleship

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.220
<i>YAMATO</i>

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:45.950
Uchuu no kanata Iscandar he...

00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:47.950
...unmei seoi...

00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.360
...ima tobitatsu

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:53.520
Kanarazu koko he...

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:56.750
...kaette kuru to

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:01.550
Te wo furu hito ni...

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:05.550
...egao de kotae

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:07.690
Ginga wo hanare...

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.150
...Iscandar he...

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.350
...harubaru nozomu

00:01:12.650 --> 00:01:19.050
Uchuu senkan Yamato

00:01:37.160 --> 00:01:44.400
In 2199, Earth was attacked by forces from
Gamilus, a mysterious planet in deep space...

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:47.670
...and mankind was on the verge of
extinction due to radioactive poisons.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.270
Planet Iscandar

00:01:49.050 --> 00:01:54.370
{CHIKYUU}There is a radioactive purifier on Iscandar,
in the Magellanic Cloud, far away from Earth.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:08.020
{SONO}The space battleship Yamato began a journey
of 148,000 light years to obtain the purifier.

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:18.420
Planet Gamilus

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:17.870
{IMA}The Yamato has left our Solar
System and is hurrying to Iscandar.

00:02:19.150 --> 00:02:29.990
Great Empire of Gamilus/
Galactic System Command Headquarters

00:02:34.920 --> 00:02:39.920
Central Planning Room

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:46.400
{1}Long live Lord Desler !

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:51.050
{2}Long live Lord Desler !

00:02:52.370 --> 00:02:55.700
{3}Long live Lord Desler !

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:00.860
{4}Long live Lord Desler !

00:03:02.470 --> 00:03:06.250
{5}Long live Lord Desler !

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.600
Lord Desler

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:12.380
You may begin.

00:03:12.970 --> 00:03:17.540
I'm going to explain the foolish
baby steps of the Yamato.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:17.820
General Hisu

00:03:18.050 --> 00:03:23.990
The Yamato left Earth on the eight
hundred and first day of Desler year 103.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:28.920
{dounen}On the eight hundred and 2nd day, it tested
its warp capability in the Mars sector.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:34.400
{chikyuu}It became the first Earth ship
ever to exceed the speed of light.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:41.810
{ikioi}The Yamato grew confident and destroyed
our base on the floating island with a "pistol."

00:03:42.150 --> 00:03:45.060
Hisu, was it a pistol ?

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.020
It's called a
Wave Motion Gun...

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.980
...but to me, it is
but a mere pistol.

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.810
I don't need your opinions.
Only report the facts.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:56.270
Yes, sir.
My apologies.

00:03:56.270 --> 00:04:03.020
In short, the Yamato has
boldly left its solar system.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.620
However Lord Desler, a minefield,
named after you...

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:10.020
General Talan

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:13.580
...has been set up as a solid defensive line in
the outer boundaries of their solar system.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:18.020
{kono}Despite being the first Earth ship
to exceed the speed of light...

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.570
{kono}...this defensive line will burn
the Yamato like a paper plane.

00:04:21.570 --> 00:04:27.170
{yuushoku}I arranged it as an
amusement after your supper.

00:04:29.770 --> 00:04:34.860
General Talan, thank you for setting
up such an interesting attraction.

00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:38.030
{KOYOI}This drink will
taste good tonight.

00:04:38.030 --> 00:04:42.400
Gentlemen, why don't we toast and pray
for the survival of the space battleship Yamato.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:49.790
For the survival of Yamato...?
Our lord likes to joke.

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:02.860
Gamilus doesn't
need such a vulgar man.

00:05:05.350 --> 00:05:07.910
Long live Lord Desler !

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.020
Unidentified object detected.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:30.070
Put it on
the video screen.

00:05:30.070 --> 00:05:31.020
Aye, sir.

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:37.230
Magnified by 700x.

00:05:40.390 --> 00:05:42.020
Launch the dummy boat.

00:05:42.640 --> 00:05:45.880
Captain, I'll use the newly
designed balloon dummy.

00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:47.160
Balloon dummy ?

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.240
That's a cute Yamato.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.200
How's my balloon dummy ?

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:52.570
They're mines.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:53.690
Don't worry, Kodai.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:57.500
If we change course,
it won't be a problem.

00:07:09.750 --> 00:07:11.980
The Yamato changed course.

00:07:15.050 --> 00:07:18.160
Looks like it's going to
go around the Desler mines.

00:07:27.280 --> 00:07:28.510
Wha...?

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:33.400
They're matching our movement.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:41.380
Just get away
by warping, Shima.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:43.170
Don't be so absurd.

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.580
We can't warp if they're
in our path, remember ?

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:49.400
Then what should we do ?

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:51.770
Shima, stop the ship.

00:07:51.770 --> 00:07:53.550
If we move carelessly,
we'll be attacked.

00:07:54.170 --> 00:07:54.850
Aye.

00:08:12.710 --> 00:08:14.500
They stopped moving, too.

00:08:15.020 --> 00:08:17.970
Mori, measure the
space between the mines.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:18.760
Aye, sir.

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:24.950
Hey Kodai, why don't you
use the Wave Motion Gun ?

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.500
No, we can't charge
the energy in time.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:29.830
You're slow.

00:08:29.830 --> 00:08:31.950
What do you mean by slow,
you mediocre driver ?!

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:33.000
Say what ?

00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.190
Because you are...

00:08:34.190 --> 00:08:35.550
Hey, stop it,
both of you !

00:08:36.060 --> 00:08:38.520
Captain, I've calculated the spacing.

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:43.750
They're 110 meters apart in both
vertical and horizontal directions.

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:46.850
We can barely make it.

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:50.150
Shima, go through
the minefield.

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:50.980
Aye, sir.

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:52.890
Start the sub-engines.

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.240
Starting the sub-engines.

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:13.900
Ahead slow.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:18.120
It's getting interesting. I'm counting
on you, Mr. Mediocre Driver.

00:09:18.120 --> 00:09:20.050
Leave it to me,
slow Chief Gunner.

00:09:38.190 --> 00:09:41.420
Your Excellency,
the show is about to begin.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:49.080
Gentlemen, do not forget your
applause at the end of the Yamato.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:29.370
Hey, how's it going,
Mediocre Driver ?

00:10:29.370 --> 00:10:31.150
Don't call me mediocre.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.840
If you aren't, get through
and prove that you aren't.

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:37.160
Damn, I'll get through,
no matter what.

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:16.170
Strange...
Hey, something's wrong.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:18.080
The mines
ahead are moving.

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:21.120
C'mon, you lay blame on
others when you can't do it ?

00:11:21.120 --> 00:11:26.110
Captain, the mines ahead are getting
closer to each other at 2cm per second.

00:11:26.110 --> 00:11:27.250
What ?  Really ?

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:38.200
The ones aft are also
moving in the same manner.

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:41.670
Captain, their antennae are
emitting an electromagnetic wave.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:46.100
Shima, be careful. If we're caught by that
electromagnetic wave, they'll explode.

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:08.030
Shima, brake.
Stop, stop.

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:09.840
No, I'll get through.

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:14.450
I know you're a good driver,
so listen to me and stop.

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:15.870
No.

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:17.600
Shima, stop the ship.

00:12:19.750 --> 00:12:21.030
Stopping the ship.

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:23.390
Stop the ship.

00:12:23.580 --> 00:12:24.420
Stopping the ship.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:30.070
Geez, are they conducting a
performance test on the engines ?

00:12:30.070 --> 00:12:31.490
Start and stop,
start and stop..

00:12:31.830 --> 00:12:36.630
Mori, there should be a
controller for the mines.  Find it.

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:37.100
Aye, sir.

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:41.240
We have to get rid of the transmitter
that controls the mines first.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:43.170
Mr. Sanada,
you take care of it.

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:43.850
Aye, sir.

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:46.520
Analyzer. Analyzer. Analyzer.

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:48.970
Sick Bay

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:47.920
Analyzer !

00:12:48.920 --> 00:12:52.620
There's no law that
prohibits a robot from drinking.

00:12:52.890 --> 00:12:55.920
Go ahead and drink.
Don't hesitate, drink.

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:59.020
I am a robot. I am not
interested in such a thing.

00:12:59.020 --> 00:13:02.830
Don't be stuck up.
I'll tell you how to taste sake.

00:13:02.830 --> 00:13:07.140
Water:  83 percent,
ethyl alcohol:  15 percent.

00:13:07.750 --> 00:13:10.950
See ?
Tastes good, doesn't it ?

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.200
Analyzer, where are you ?

00:13:13.200 --> 00:13:15.580
Get to the
Explorer at once.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:18.170
Analyzer, you have a job.

00:13:21.830 --> 00:13:23.760
They sure work us hard.

00:13:31.770 --> 00:13:33.080
Here I am.

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:35.640
Analyzer, you slacker.

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:40.370
That's it.

00:13:41.350 --> 00:13:44.610
There's an irregular transmission
from 5 degrees high.

00:13:45.200 --> 00:13:49.170
Mr. Sanada, investigate the
mine 5 degrees high from the Yamato.

00:13:49.170 --> 00:13:50.360
Understood, Captain.

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:52.830
I'm launching.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:10.630
Analyzer, find the control
mine as soon as possible.

00:14:10.630 --> 00:14:11.840
Aye, sir.

00:14:23.540 --> 00:14:25.840
T...they're acting strange.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:29.420
They must be searching
for the control mine.

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.260
Any commander
would do that.

00:14:37.630 --> 00:14:39.340
They're closer by 20cm.

00:14:39.680 --> 00:14:40.770
Oh no.

00:14:40.770 --> 00:14:42.840
At this rate, the ship will interfere
with that electromagnetic wave.

00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:45.750
Mr. Sanada, haven't you
found the control mine yet ?

00:14:45.750 --> 00:14:47.300
Not yet.
Please wait.

00:14:48.420 --> 00:14:50.720
Captain, we're in danger.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.690
Shima, tilt the ship.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:55.360
Five degrees to port.

00:14:55.360 --> 00:14:56.400
Y...yes, sir.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:59.790
Can't you hear my orders ?!
You idiot, tilt the ship !

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.520
Aye, sir !
Tilting the ship...

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:04.520
...five degrees to port.

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.580
Analyzer, haven't
you found it yet ?

00:15:19.580 --> 00:15:25.100
Due to the electromagnetic waves,
I can't filter out the control wave.

00:15:25.990 --> 00:15:27.170
Don't make excuses.

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:29.170
You got drunk
when we need you most.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:32.340
Damn, a useless part of
you is so precisely made.

00:15:32.340 --> 00:15:35.160
Hurry up. If we take too long,
the Yamato will explode.

00:15:36.340 --> 00:15:38.420
Space mines,
closer by 15cm.

00:15:38.420 --> 00:15:40.030
Bank angle, plus 5 degrees.

00:15:40.030 --> 00:15:41.300
Bank angle, plus 5 degrees.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.350
Aihara, haven't you
heard from Mr. Sanada ?

00:15:44.350 --> 00:15:46.420
Nothing yet.

00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:49.750
Bank angle,
plus 10 degrees.

00:16:00.400 --> 00:16:03.000
An irregular transmission is coming
from the mine to the right.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:05.520
That's it.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:18.730
Analyzer, find the transmitter.

00:16:18.730 --> 00:16:19.600
Roger.

00:16:23.740 --> 00:16:25.900
Don't mess up, Analyzer.

00:16:25.900 --> 00:16:27.120
I'm alright.

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:37.830
Space mine,
closer by 10cm.

00:16:37.830 --> 00:16:39.360
Plus five degrees.

00:16:39.890 --> 00:16:43.710
Mr. Shima, please be careful.
A mine to port is too close.

00:16:43.710 --> 00:16:46.700
Captain, this's as
much as we can roll.

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:50.800
Captain...?

00:16:57.750 --> 00:16:59.700
Done yet ?  Hurry !  The Yamato
doesn't have much time !

00:17:00.600 --> 00:17:01.880
I found it.

00:17:03.510 --> 00:17:05.900
It's being transmitted
from this cone.

00:17:06.610 --> 00:17:10.850
Good. Remove the cap.
Don't shake it.

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:11.680
Roger.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:18.230
Are you really alright ?

00:17:18.230 --> 00:17:20.720
I'm 100,000 times more
precise than a human.

00:17:20.720 --> 00:17:21.740
Shut up.

00:17:22.840 --> 00:17:24.770
Yamato, Yamato...

00:17:24.770 --> 00:17:26.600
This is Yamato.

00:17:26.600 --> 00:17:28.920
I've found
the control mine.

00:17:29.740 --> 00:17:31.110
Disassembly is in progress.

00:17:31.110 --> 00:17:31.770
Roger.

00:17:35.180 --> 00:17:37.860
No orders for
30 minutes from up there.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:40.270
What is our Captain thinking ?

00:17:49.100 --> 00:17:53.630
Yes, steady. Slowly.
You pull it straight, okay.

00:17:54.390 --> 00:17:56.450
I'm alright. Trust me.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.450
You did it, Analyzer.

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:21.790
Hey Analyzer, one mistake,
and it'll go off with a bang.

00:18:21.790 --> 00:18:23.480
I'm analyzing.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:35.270
I found it. That's it.

00:18:37.070 --> 00:18:38.250
Hey, not yet ?

00:18:47.220 --> 00:18:48.480
See, I removed it.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:52.190
Good, well done, Analyzer.

00:19:06.560 --> 00:19:08.220
Disassembly complete.

00:19:08.220 --> 00:19:09.670
The mines stopped moving.

00:19:09.670 --> 00:19:11.130
The electromagnetic
wave has stopped.

00:19:11.130 --> 00:19:13.710
Alright, Mr. Sanada,
get back immediately.

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:14.770
Kodai.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:15.720
Yes, sir ?

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.770
You lead the
Black Tiger Squadron...

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:21.460
...and remove the
mines with your hands.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.270
Aye, sir.
With our hands...

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:27.950
You mean, with this hand ?

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:31.750
Aye, sir.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:05.570
Look Shima, I'll make
a path for you, soon.

00:20:05.570 --> 00:20:06.940
Thanks for your trouble.

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:08.770
Not really.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:12.350
It's light, 'cause there's no gravity.
They're nothing for a human to move.

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:22.850
Hisu.

00:20:22.850 --> 00:20:24.110
Your Excellency...?

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:29.510
I'm a little forgetful lately.
What were those mines called ?

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:33.580
We named them after you,
and called them "Desler Mines."

00:20:33.580 --> 00:20:38.300
It's a serious offense to disgrace your name.
I'll take any punishment.

00:20:43.640 --> 00:20:46.770
Hisu, you don't have to be
so critical of yourself.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:48.720
I'm just astonished.

00:20:48.720 --> 00:20:51.050
They removed the
space mines by hand.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:56.170
The Desler Mines are the product
of our superior Gamilus science...

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:58.930
...but it wasn't prepared to
deal with such a foolish action.

00:21:00.240 --> 00:21:05.170
{MATTAKU}I'm learning a lot from the
primitive ideas of these barbarians.

00:21:05.170 --> 00:21:06.950
{MATTAKU}Don't you think so, gentlemen ?

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:29.670
Captain, we're ready to go.

00:21:29.670 --> 00:21:32.000
Good. Start the sub-engines.

00:21:32.000 --> 00:21:34.000
Aye, sir.
Starting the sub-engines.

00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:37.030
Start the sub-engines !

00:21:49.970 --> 00:21:54.050
Although we didn't see the end of the Yamato,
the show was quite amusing.

00:21:54.050 --> 00:21:58.350
Gentlemen, I appreciate
your consideration.

00:21:58.350 --> 00:22:02.270
I'm going to sleep.
Goodnight, gentlemen.

00:22:02.710 --> 00:22:04.840
Long live Lord Desler !

00:22:05.940 --> 00:22:09.220
Oh, Hisu, what's the name
of the captain of the Yamato ?

00:22:09.220 --> 00:22:11.640
It's Okita.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:13.170
Okita, huh ?

00:22:13.170 --> 00:22:17.020
Send a congratulatory message,
that he did well, in my name.

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:18.840
Yes, Lord Desler.

00:22:31.070 --> 00:22:32.480
A message from Gamilus.

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:38.520
Aihara, why did
you break contact ?

00:22:40.170 --> 00:22:42.880
You could have
found the source.

00:22:43.760 --> 00:22:45.370
I'm sorry.

00:22:45.370 --> 00:22:46.250
It's alright.

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:49.790
Captain, what does it say ?

00:22:49.790 --> 00:22:50.770
Aihara, read it.

00:22:51.250 --> 00:22:53.770
Crew of the Yamato,
I congratulate your performance.

00:22:53.770 --> 00:22:57.640
I look forward to future combat.
Emperor of Gamilus, Lord Desler.

00:22:57.640 --> 00:23:00.720
Desler ?  That's the
name of the enemy leader.

00:23:00.720 --> 00:23:03.200
Damn, it's getting interesting.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:08.900
Start the Wave Motion engine !
Ahead flank !

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:20.030
Hurry to Iscandar, Yamato.

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:24.030
Earth is nearing its end.

00:23:24.030 --> 00:23:27.260
Yamato, when will you return ?

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:31.050
Mankind will be extinct in 311 days.

00:23:31.050 --> 00:23:34.960
Mankind will be extinct in 311 days.

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:39.150
311 days till the destruction of Earth

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:45.600
Okita Juzo:

00:23:40.460 --> 00:23:45.600
Naya Goro

00:23:44.560 --> 00:23:53.160
Anoko ga futteita makka na scarf

00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:51.100
Mori Yuki:

00:23:45.880 --> 00:23:51.100
Asagami Yoko

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:56.610
Aihara Giichi:

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:56.610
Nomura Shinji

00:23:53.160 --> 00:24:01.960
Dareno tame da to omotte iruka

00:23:57.150 --> 00:24:06.640
Note:
Starting this episode, the skin color of Gamilusians was changed to blue.

00:23:57.150 --> 00:24:06.640
In the story, it was due to the change of the light, and the walking scene of Desler was made accordingly.

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:10.260
Dare no tame demo ii ja nai ka

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:16.640
Note:
However, the scene was not even discussed in Yamato related books, and people believed the

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:16.640
joke theory, presented in the Yamato special Q&A in the June 1977 issue of OUT magazine.

00:24:10.260 --> 00:24:19.160
Minna sono ki de ireba ii

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:22.640
Note:
Second navigator Ohta handed over the
message from Desler.

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:22.640
They mistakenly drew Ohta, instead of Aihara, and they didn't even have time to correct it.

00:24:16.640 --> 00:24:22.640
Translator's Note:
Aihara is credited twice.

